# Contour Education — Senior Software Engineer — Supplementary Questions

## Why do you want to be a Senior Software Engineer at Contour?

I have built training from scratch. I hold a Certificate IV in Training and Assessment, I have taught, and I have designed curriculum, so I understand the thing Contour is actually optimising for, which is a student moving from confused to confident. Most engineers do not have that lens, and it changes which problems I think are worth solving and which edge cases actually matter.

The engineering reality is the other half of the appeal. Contour is bootstrapped and serving more than 10,000 students on a Next.js and Go stack, which means scaling a recording-heavy Learning Portal through exam-season concurrency spikes without a war chest to absorb mistakes. Building lean and making every architectural call earn its place is exactly the engineering I do best and want to keep doing. While I've previously been focused on backend development, I would look forward to the opportunity to work full stack, leveraging my previous front end experience and building my knowledge across the full stack. 

